{"name":"Corvette","hex":"#e9ba81","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Corvette","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of sports car, manufactured by Chevrolet from 1953 to present."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Corvette"}],"entries":[{"title":"Corvette","blocks":[{"text":"A corvette is a small warship. It is traditionally the smallest class of vessel considered to be rated a warship. The warship class above the corvette is that of the frigate, while the class below was historically that of the sloop-of-war."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Zarechny_%28parade%29.jpg/330px-Zarechny_%28parade%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corvette"},{"title":"Corvette (video game)","blocks":[{"text":"Corvette is a 2003 racing video game developed by Steel Monkeys and published by TDK Mediactive for Windows, Xbox, and Game Boy Advance, and by Global Star Software for PlayStation 2 and later prints of the Xbox version. The GBA version was developed by Visual Impact. The game is based on the Chevrolet Corvette sports car in celebration of the line's 50th anniversary, and lets players race in all five generations of Corvette that existed at the time."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/92/Corvette_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corvette_(video_game)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/80-G-289820_HMCS_Riviere_du_Loup_%28K_357%29.jpg/500px-80-G-289820_HMCS_Riviere_du_Loup_%28K_357%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2e/80-G-289820_HMCS_Riviere_du_Loup_%28K_357%29.jpg/1280px-80-G-289820_HMCS_Riviere_du_Loup_%28K_357%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=pa